From 00cde7088d3744c6e820219250f26930de6860b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:11:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] [drop] look worklist glue up by signature before naming
 it

WorklistGlue::function names a glue function with a hash of its printed
signature. It printed and hashed the signature at every request, also
when the function existed already, and a module asks for the same glue
at every drop site. The printed text grows with the nesting of the type
(records of records, closures), so the cost is the number of requests
times the length of the signature.

The expansion run now keeps the glue it has resolved: DropGlueSymbols
holds the run's SymbolTableCollection and a map from (module, function
type, role attribute) to the glue function. The keys are uniqued IR
handles, so a hit prints nothing. A miss names the function and looks
it up in the symbol table as before, so the names and the emitted IR do
not change. The map has the lifetime and the rules of the tables next to it:
the pass creates it for one run over one module, the run is single
threaded (a module pass with the greedy driver), and the pass neither
erases nor renames functions. Without a caller's collection the glue is
resolved by name at every request, as before.

Measured on aarch64 Linux (20 cores, shared machine, load 3 to 13), rrc
-O aggressive, one process at a time, warm polyffi cache, median of 3
runs (minimum in parentheses), before -> after:

A 6.0 MB program of a compiler that targets Reussir (3794 functions,
nested polymorphic records and closures):
  ReussirAcquireDropExpansionPass, both runs   35.8 s -> 5.1 s (35.1 -> 5.0)
  MLIR lowering pipeline                       83.6 s -> 53.9 s (83.1 -> 53.7)
  source to executable                         116.7 s -> 84.4 s (112.5 -> 83.6)
The object file and the executable are byte-identical.

Six more programs of that compiler, 0.1 MB to 2.7 MB of source, spend
0.02 s to 0.8 s in the pass before and after (differences inside the run
to run variation), and 1.2 s to 35 s from source to executable, unchanged;
their object files and executables are byte-identical.

core, std and the 31 programs of reussir-lang/benchmark (-Oaggressive
--reuse-across-call --relocation-mode pic): the lowered MLIR of all 33
units is byte-identical. The pass takes 0.27 s -> 0.23 s on std and
0.13 s -> 0.15 s on mltt, the two largest units: no measurable change.

No test is added: the change has no observable but compile time. The
lit tests selected by 'worklist|drop|ffi|tagged|bigint|rcgmp|leaf|integer'
give the same results as before the change, and reussir-ut passes.
Formatted with clang-format 23.1.0 on the changed lines.
